# Hindi Imposition - The Anger of the Southern People!

## Members of Parliament Who Wrote to Nehru About This

1. N. Sivaraj
2. E. V. K. Sampath
3. R. Dharmalingam
4. Dr Krishnasamy
5. Mohammed Imam (Mysore)
6. A. M. Barua (Assam)
7. Babasaheb
8. Mulgaonkar
9. Shanmuga Gounder
10. N. Bharucha
11. Jaipal Singh (Bihar)
12. Maharaja Karni Singh (Bikaner)
13. K. Gaikwad
14. M. S. Sugandhi
15. P. R. Malgankar

Dear friends,

Have no doubt. Hindi will not be imposed, and my assurance will be fulfilled. The President has also spoken on this matter.

Yours,

Jawaharlal Nehru

Comrade Sivaraj, MP, reports that Pandit Nehru sent a letter in this form in response to the letter from the fifteen Members of Parliament.

(*Seithi*, 7 August 1960; *Dravida Nadu*)
